## Ownership at the destination

- **Ownership is by batch.** An item at `{{ destination }}`, or at a destination a kind
  routes to, belongs to the batch its `{{ namespace }}` record says created it. A comment
  belongs to the batch its marker names. This batch, `{{ batch }}`, may create, edit (by
  staging its ticket again with `onefollowup ticket copy`) or withdraw only items it
  created, and may edit only comments whose marker names `{{ batch }}`. It never changes an
  item or a comment belonging to another batch, but for the one write below:
  `onefollowup ticket re-estimate` on that item.
- **`onefollowup ticket re-estimate` re-estimates an item's priority after this batch
  comments on it.** It recounts the item's occurrences from its comments, stores the
  estimate in its `{{ namespace }}` record, rewrites the `- Priority estimate:` line of its
  `## Impact` section, and moves its priority only while the destination holds the estimate
  its record stored (or holds none, where it stored none), so a priority a person set
  stays. It changes nothing else about the item, its status included. Stage it on the item
  each time this batch adds or edits an evidence comment there, and on no other occasion.
- **An evidence comment** carries this batch's evidence on another batch's item.
  `onefollowup ticket comment` gives it its visible opening line and its closing marker,
  naming this batch and the item's root cause; you write only what goes between.

  **It carries only this batch's new occurrence**, because the item already states the
  ticket and a comment that re-renders it hides the one new fact it adds. Its body is, in
  this order:

  1. this batch's occurrence: the host it was verified on, read with `hostname`; the basis
     commit of each repository; what was observed; and the drafts or inputs it rests on;
  2. one short paragraph headed in plain text `Bears on the ticket:`, naming the section of
     the item the new evidence contradicts or extends (its root cause, impact or suggested
     fix) and stating only the delta, since this batch cannot edit another batch's ticket.
     It is optional, but **required where this batch's evidence shows the root cause
     broader than the item states**, and then states only the widened root cause, in the
     same plain words a ticket's `## Root cause` is written in, and names each location it
     adds as a contributing location of the suggested fix. A batch widens its own item by
     rewriting its ticket and staging it again instead.

  It never repeats what the item already says — its root cause, impact, examples,
  suggested fix, rejected fixes or owning batches — and never carries one of a ticket's
  level-2 section headings. `onefollowup ticket comment` refuses a body that carries one.

  It goes only on an open item another batch created for the same root cause, which
  receives at most **one** from this batch, whatever open status the destination holds it
  at, so an item at a deferred status receives this batch's one comment like any other open
  item. Where this batch's evidence comment is already there, edit it in place with
  `onefollowup ticket comment`; never add a second. This batch never adds an evidence
  comment to an item it created: it edits that item by staging its ticket again instead.
